! AlAs with an ultrasoft dataset on both species: the Born charge of a **polar**
! crystal, which is the one thing `si-epsilon-us.in` cannot measure.
!
! Silicon's `Z*` is zero by symmetry, so the -0.07945 both codes print there is a
! basis-set residue and the 8e-6 agreement is between two codes' errors. AlAs is
! zincblende, so `Z*` is a real charge of order 2 with opposite signs on the two
! species, and `constraint_position_term` -- worth 0.55 on silicon, seven times
! the answer it is added to -- is finally compared against something of its own
! size.
!
! The cell, cutoffs and datasets are `alas-us.in`'s, whose bands are validated
! against Elk along L-Gamma-X (0.062 eV rms on the valence manifold). Symmetry is
! left on and the grid is shifted, both as in `si-epsilon-us.in`, so that the two
! ultrasoft cases differ in the crystal alone.
!
! `ecutrho` is 8 x `ecutwfc`: the augmentation charge is sharply peaked and is
! not representable on a dual-4 grid.
!
! **What it found, since a case's header should say that and not only what it was
! written for**: the antisymmetric part was wrong by 1.4e-2 on a charge of 3.3,
! because the term that carries it is quadratic in a per-k tangent and its wedge
! sum had never been completed (`PLAN.md` P39a). PAW was refused for that same
! error, measured on a wedge and read as a missing one-centre term, and that
! refusal is gone.
!
! The reference is regenerated with the vendored `ph.x` (`alas-epsilon-us.ph.in`)
! and committed as `reference.out.ph-alas-epsilon-us`.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.575, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 25.0, ecutrho = 200.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
    mixing_beta = 0.7
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al  26.98  Al.pbe-n-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF
 As  74.92  As.pbe-n-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Al 0.00 0.00 0.00
 As 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 4 4 4 1 1 1
